## 1. Before you contribute

Read `README.md` (what {{ project_name }} is), `CLAUDE.md` (the inherited invariants and
process rules), and this file before writing code.

## 2. Set up a development environment

```bash
git clone https://github.com/{{ github_owner }}/{{ project_slug }}.git
cd {{ project_slug }}

# Install uv if you don't have it: https://github.com/astral-sh/uv
just setup            # uv venv --python {{ python_version }} + uv pip install -e '.[dev]'

# Verify
uv run {{ project_slug }} --help || uv run python -m {{ module_name }}
just gates            # full local gate suite
```

Python **{{ python_version }}** is the baseline for every command, venv, hook, script, and
test. There is no fallback to an older interpreter.

## 3. Workflow

1. **Open an issue first** for non-trivial changes.
2. **Branch from `main`** (`<type>/<short-description>`, e.g. `feat/foo`, `fix/bar`).
3. **One thing per PR.**
4. **Run the gates locally** before pushing: `just gates`.
5. **Open a PR** and fill out the template. The audit checklist is non-negotiable.
6. **Never commit directly to `main`.**

## 4. Change governance

Any change that is **not surgical** (diff > ~150 LOC or > ~8 files, labelled `major`, or
touching a designated core path) requires a **decision record** in `docs/decisions/` before
code. Copy `docs/decisions/TEMPLATE.md`; it must contain a scored `## Options (A/B/C scored)`
comparison, a `## Steelman`, and `## Pressure-test evidence` from an isolated `/tmp` run. CI
blocks the PR if the record is missing or malformed.

## 5. Coding style

- Python {{ python_version }}, typed (`mypy --strict`), formatted (`ruff format`), linted (`ruff check`)
- Every public function has a Google-style docstring
- Specific exceptions, not bare `except` or broad `except Exception`
- Subprocess: list-form args, explicit `timeout`, `shell=False`
- All datetimes timezone-aware UTC
- an `SPDX-License-Identifier` header set to `{{ license }}` on every source file (`reuse lint` enforces this)

## 6. Testing

- Every test runs every time. No `@pytest.mark.skip` carve-outs.
- Coverage minimum is **{{ coverage_min }}%**, enforced by `just test`.
- Error paths and boundary values are tested, not just happy paths.

## 7. Dependencies

Adding a runtime dependency requires PR justification: it must replace meaningful code, be
actively maintained, carry a redistribution-compatible license (no GPL/AGPL/LGPL), and have a
recognizable maintainer. `pip-audit` must pass.

## 8. Security

If you find a vulnerability, **do not open a public issue.** See [`SECURITY.md`](SECURITY.md).
Insecure shortcuts are forbidden even when requested.

## 9. Commits

Conventional Commits: `<type>(<scope>): <subject>`. Types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `test`,
`refactor`, `build`, `ci`, `chore`, `perf`, `security`.

## 10. License

By contributing you confirm you have authority to contribute the material and agree it is
licensed under **{{ license }}**. Every first-party source file carries:

```
SPDX-License-Identifier: {{ license }}
```

## 11. Code of Conduct

See [`CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md`](CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md). Be respectful, assume good faith, focus on the code.
